{"task_id": "HumanEval/24", "solution": "import math\n\ndef largest_divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\" For a given number n, find the largest number that divides n evenly, smaller than n\n    >>> largest_divisor(15)\n    5\n    \"\"\"\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return n // 2\n    \n    # For odd numbers, iterate from sqrt(n) down to 3 (step 2) to find the largest factor.\n    # The largest proper divisor will be n // i for the smallest odd factor i > 1,\n    # or 1 if n is prime.\n    r = int(math.isqrt(n))\n    for i in range(r, 1, -2): # Iterate downwards for efficiency (find largest divisor sooner)\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return n // i\n            \n    # If no divisor found other than 1 and n itself, n is prime.\n    # The largest proper divisor for a prime number is 1.\n    return 1"}
